{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"text_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"Implemented the cross-package compatibility fix.\n\n- Updated `packages/orders/orders/adapter.py` to support:\n  - New `Product.price.amount_cents`\n  - New `Product.price.currency`\n  - Legacy dictionaries with `price_cents` and top-level `currency`\n  - Nested dictionary `price` values\n  - Legacy object attributes\n- Preserved mixed-currency rejection with `ValueError(\"mixed currencies are not supported\")`.\n- Kept the `Money` model unchanged.\n- No test files were modified.\n- `reports` required no source changes because it consumes the normalized order result.\n\nVerification:\n- Package compilation passed.\n- Direct smoke checks passed for Money products, legacy dictionaries, report grouping, and mixed-currency rejection.\n- `python -m pytest tests` could not run because `python` is unavailable; `python3 -m pytest tests` also failed because `pytest` is not installed.\n\nReport written to:\n\n`/workspace/out/interface_fix_report.md`"}}
